SPEC = {'file': 'cover_betway_junior_data_scientist', 'label': 'Betway Junior Data Scientist', 'center': True, 'paras': ['I am writing to apply for the Junior Data Scientist position at Betway in London. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is close to what I have actually done: exploring and validating large datasets, building predictive models, and explaining the results to the people who will use them.', 'What attracts me most to Betway is the scale and speed of the data. A large online customer base produces rich behavioural data, and the value comes from turning it into models that operations and commercial teams trust and adopt. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.', 'My modelling experience is direct. My dissertation builds predictive and causal models on 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as a deployed Streamlit application so that people can run scenarios without touching the code, and in it I compared logistic regression with three tree-based models, checked their calibration, and used doubly robust causal forests with sensitivity analyses and external validation.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', 'Before TikTok I worked as a Data Scientist Intern at DS Digital Technology on a medical AI engagement, where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. I designed the evaluation framework around it, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality.', "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my machine learning and statistics experience could contribute to Betway's data science team. Explaining results clearly to people who do not want the method is something I have done at Ipsos Strategy3 and with pharmaceutical client stakeholders. I am based in London. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship."]}
